Task: review-fixes (conductor-review of track aguihitl_20260908)

Verdict was Request changes on one High finding; this commit closes it
plus both Mediums.

High — duplicate interrupt ids across multiple input requests:
  agui/internal/stream/processor.go inputRequestFrom now requires
  ev.RequestedInput.InterruptID == fc.ID before preferring the typed
  request. Verified red first: two calls produced two interrupts both
  with id 'input-a'.

  Impact chain traced during review: duplicate ids reach
  RecordsFromInterrupts, then ValidateResumeAgainstPending's pendingByID
  map collapses them, so a resume answering one id satisfies the
  'all pending addressed' check while the second workflow node waits
  forever.

  Root cause: FR1 (prefer typed RequestedInput) and FR3 (collect all
  interrupts) were implemented in phases P3 and P2 respectively, and no
  test exercised both at once. Worth remembering as a pattern — the
  defect was in the interaction, not in either phase's own code.

Medium — untested behaviour change:
  TestProcessEvent_PlainToolCallAfterInterrupt pins that a plain tool
  call sharing an event with an interrupt is emitted (previously dropped
  when ProcessEvent returned early) and receives no TOOL_CALL_RESULT.
  Deliberately characterization, not a fix.

Medium — public API doc gap:
  WithInterruptReasonClassifier godoc now states it is ignored under
  WithExecutor, matching WithGenAIPartConverter's existing warning.

Verification: inputRequestFrom back to 100% coverage; gofmt -l silent,
go vet ./... silent, CI=true go test ./... all packages ok.
